  "notes": "To divide and hand out shares of something to multiple recipients. Commonly used in economic, business, and organizational contexts for distributing profits, resources, or tasks.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {利益|りえき}{分配|ぶんぱい}: profit distribution\n- {富|とみ}の{分配|ぶんぱい}: distribution of wealth\n- {均等|きんとう}に{分配|ぶんぱい}する: to distribute equally\n- {分配|ぶんぱい}{金|きん}: dividend; distributed funds\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {配分|はいぶん}する: to allot; to apportion — more formal, often used for budgets and resources\n- {配|くば}る: to hand out; to distribute — more everyday, physical distribution\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}する: to divide; to split — focuses on the act of dividing, not necessarily giving shares to others",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
